## Facts
- Final node 7-sample gate on current packages: SupportChat.Ts passed individually (29 s) and 2/2 in
  round 1, but the aggregate `bash samples/run_samples.sh` (order TicTacToe → Bingo → DeliveryDispatch
  → SupportChat …) failed at SupportChat with THREE simultaneous
  `ZlinkStreamException: Wait for stream message timed out.` from the browser scenario
  (`scripts/browser-e2e/run-sample.mjs:63`), log `zlink-work/c016/logs/gate-final-samples-node-aggregate-2.log:270-300`
  (heartbeat pings from client-3..7 keep flowing until the three waits expire — the connections are
  alive, the awaited messages never arrive). So round 1's budget change did not remove the race; it is
  the same family: waits armed after the awaited notification was delivered (or delivered to a
  session the scenario has already replaced), i.e. a scenario/sample ordering defect — or a real
  framework delivery gap after reconnect (bound-session push to the resumed session).
- Decide with evidence, not budgets: preserve the browser log + OTel flow files
  (`/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-node/zlink-supportchat.ts-*/logs/flow/`) of a failing run; identify WHICH three
  waits expired (`supportchat-client-scenario.ts` line numbers) and, for each, whether the server
  emitted the message (flow `dispatched/replied` on the server, `stream-inbound` on the gateway) before
  or after the wait was armed and to which session (old vs resumed). Compare with the cpp/dotnet/java
  SupportChat clients (read-only) for how they order "arm wait → act" around reconnect/resume.
- Reproduce: run the aggregate order (`bash samples/run_samples.sh TicTacToe.Ts Bingo.Ts DeliveryDispatch.Ts SupportChat.Ts`
  if the runner accepts a list, else the four sequentially) up to 4×, and SupportChat alone 3×, to get
  the determinism table.

## What to do
1. Root cause with `file:line` and the sample contract clause (message semantics / idle+close
   lifecycle / resume) that the scenario or the framework violates.
2. Fix minimally: if the scenario arms waits too late, restructure the scenario so every wait is
   armed before the action that triggers it (and resumed sessions observe state via the contract's
   resume/replay, not by hoping to catch an in-flight notify); if the framework drops a push to a
   resumed session, fix `packages/framework/**` with a contract test under `test/contract/`.
3. Verify: aggregate order 3× green, SupportChat alone 2× green, `node --test test/contract/sample-supportchat-message-semantics-gate.test.js`
   green, and the full `bash samples/run_samples.sh` once (all 7, exit 0).

